<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal details BTA stake selloff.</title>
<headline>Portugal details BTA stake selloff.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Portuguese government said on Thursday it planned to sell 6.3 million shares of Banco Totta e Acores (BTA) by national and international direct sale.</p>
<p>It would also sell some 1.6 million shares in BTA via a public offer to sell (OPV) on the Lisbon bourse, according to a statement issued after a weekly cabinet meeting.</p>
<p>These included 635,000 shares for employees, 465,000 for small investors and emigrants, and 500,000 for the general public.</p>
<p>The government is expected to sell its 13.22 percent stake in BTA in November.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +351-1-3538254</p>
